From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cts: latency balancing times the clock network without CRPR
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The latency balancers read clock arrivals at the sinks, which clock
reconvergence pessimism removal does not change. With CRPR on, every
register clock pin's arrival carries its own clock path, the clock
network's tags do not merge, and the arrivals the balancers ask for grow
with the design: on XiangShan's XSTile Top (700k registers) they took
77 GB and most of CTS's runtime.

Turn CRPR off while the balancers run and restore it after, before
useful skew's budget reads slacks; restoring it invalidates the arrivals.
The tree is unchanged: XSTile's Top writes a byte-identical checkpoint,
CTS peaks at 51.5 GiB instead of 117-123 GiB, in 761 s instead of 1,325 s.

Carried in bazel-orfs, not upstreamed; retires with the //:bump onto an
OpenROAD that has it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 src/cts/src/TritonCTS.cpp | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/cts/src/TritonCTS.cpp b/src/cts/src/TritonCTS.cpp
index bf3f5d9a56..ade57b5ea4 100644
--- a/src/cts/src/TritonCTS.cpp
+++ b/src/cts/src/TritonCTS.cpp
@@ -64,6 +64,26 @@ namespace cts {
 
 using utl::CTS;
 
+namespace {
+
+// Turns clock reconvergence pessimism removal off for its scope.
+class CrprDisabled
+{
+ public:
+  explicit CrprDisabled(sta::dbSta* sta)
+      : sta_(sta), was_enabled_(sta->crprEnabled())
+  {
+    sta_->setCrprEnabled(false);
+  }
+  ~CrprDisabled() { sta_->setCrprEnabled(was_enabled_); }
+
+ private:
+  sta::dbSta* sta_;
+  const bool was_enabled_;
+};
+
+}  // namespace
+
 TritonCTS::TritonCTS(utl::Logger* logger,
                      odb::dbDatabase* db,
                      sta::dbNetwork* network,
@@ -2788,6 +2808,14 @@ int TritonCTS::runLatencyBalancers(double capPerDBU,
                                    double resPerDBU,
                                    bool useful_skew)
 {
+  // The balancers read clock arrivals only, which clock reconvergence
+  // pessimism removal does not change. With it on, every register clock
+  // pin's arrival carries its own clock path, so the clock network's
+  // arrivals do not merge: on a 700k-register design they took 77 GB.
+  // Turning it back on invalidates the arrivals, so the slacks read after
+  // balancing (useful skew's budget, repair) have it.
+  CrprDisabled crpr_disabled(openSta_);
+
   int totalDelayBuff = 0;
   for (auto& builder : std::ranges::reverse_view(builders_)) {
     if (builder->getParent() == nullptr && !builder->getChildren().empty()) {
